      "content": "idk i just feel like they'd find a way around \"health codes\" if the profit was high enough. like, what if it wasn't a heavy drug, but just something like a scent-based compound that mimics the smell of fresh baked goods or something that affects the brain super subtly? wouldn't that be harder to track than a \"dangerous\" stimulant? it's just hard to believe it's all just \"marketing\" when it feels so much more physical than that.",
